# Template for the untracked talos/local/cluster.local.env (that folder is git-ignored).
# Copy it there and set the value. render.sh reads it after cluster.env, so it overrides it.
#
# Needed whenever the short name in cluster.env (ENDPOINT_HOST=mini01) does not resolve from the
# node being built. A worker booted from the ISO in maintenance mode cannot resolve "mini01"
# (seen on mini03's first boot), so render with the control plane's LAN address instead.
# Use the LAN address of the control plane (mini01) as seen from the new node; look it up on the
# router. It is not a secret, but decision D2 keeps addresses out of tracked files, so the real
# value lives only in the untracked copy.
ENDPOINT_HOST=<control-plane-lan-address>
